  'BUILD RECORD, step 2, the heads-up email (built 2026-11-02, waiting for Sean''s approval; nothing has been sent to a host). On the outreach engine: the list is ve_outreach_cities ''event-hosts'' (kind people, program event-heads-up, switched off, daily cap 30) and the email is ve_outreach_templates event-heads-up step 1 (draft). A host is the Directory listing that hosts the events (events.host_listing_id): ve_event_host_contacts, rebuilt by ve_event_hosts_refresh() from the calendar; its email is the one it publishes (the group contact ve-groups find_contact reads from their own site, else their Instagram bio, else the listing''s email), with where it was found; status active, no_email, held (London: business addresses only, ve_is_free_mail), has_account (owned listing or Group Partner), stopped (unsubscribed or by the team). ve_event_heads_up_due(): active, not suppressed, not emailed in 14 days, with new events (ve_event_host_new_events: approved, ours, 2 to 120 days out, not organized or claimed, not named before; up to 8, grouped). Sender: edge function ve-event-headsup, cron every 15 minutes, weekdays 10 AM to 5 PM Eastern, only with the email approved and the list on; email-send brand vegans-explore (one-click unsubscribe is the brand suppression, permanent), signed by the chapter''s active Community Manager else the Vegans Explore team, never Sean''s name, no prices (template_save refuses prices and Sean''s name); each event its own tracked link (/go/eh-..., initiative event-heads-up); every send a ve_event_headsups row; campaign ve-event-headsup-<date> in HQ > Email. Depot > Events > Heads-up (#headsup, #headsup/email, #headsup/edit, #headsup/host/<id>): the switch, the email as a host gets it, Send me a test, Approve this email (switches it on), Change the words (back to draft and paused), each host with Find their email, an email typed with where it is published, Never email them. Migration 20261102_event_heads_up.sql (applied through the connector); ve-event-headsup from commit 91d3db4, sha256 matched. Proven live: unauthenticated tick and overview refused; the tick held (not approved); Find email found info@ppmny.org (their contact page), info@cfvegfest.org and Philly Vegan Social Club''s Gmail (Instagram bio), Veg Society of DC''s site did not open, London Vegans'' site has none; preview rendered (London Vegan Meetup, 8 events grouped, signed by the team); two tests to contact@lesaruss.com (London Vegan Meetup, Philly Vegan Social Club) with no rows or links written; a price in the words refused; switching on before approval refused. On 2026-11-02: 15 hosts, 3 with a published email. Next: Sean approves the email once; then the door Guides on the Vegan Events Guide.',
  'text', 'decision'
